# The orchestrator's settings (surakshasetu/config.py). Copy this file to orchestrator/.env
# (gitignored): the uncommented values below are the local stack's and work as they are with
# `make up` + `make gateway-up`. Settings reads .env from the working directory, and every make
# target runs the orchestrator from orchestrator/. A real environment variable beats the file.
#
# A value set here no longer follows the code's default: when a step changes a default (Step 9
# moved the gateway from :8090 to :20130), update your .env too. Commented lines are optional or
# must stay unset in dev. Never put a real secret in this file. Outside dev (SS_ENV=pilot or prod)
# every setting in REQUIRED_OUTSIDE_DEV must be set explicitly.

# dev | test | pilot | prod
SS_ENV=dev

# Postgres as app_rw. Required outside dev.
SS_PG_DSN_APP=postgresql://app_rw:surakshasetu-dev-app-rw@127.0.0.1:5432/surakshasetu

# Valkey/Redis (used from Step 16). Required outside dev.
SS_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0

# domain-services. The token is required outside dev.
SS_DOMAIN_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
SS_DOMAIN_TOKEN=surakshasetu-dev-domain-token

# Subject keys (Step 4). The KEK is base64 of 32 bytes; this dev value is public. In prod the KEK
# lives in an India-region KMS/HSM. Both required outside dev.
SS_KEK_B64=c3VyYWtzaGFzZXR1LWRldi1rZWstbm90LXNlY3JldCE=
SS_PG_DSN_KEYVAULT=postgresql://keyvault_rw:surakshasetu-dev-keyvault-rw@127.0.0.1:5432/surakshasetu

# Audit anchoring (Step 4). MinIO credentials match infra/.env's MINIO_ROOT_*. Retention is in
# days of COMPLIANCE object lock. All required outside dev.
SS_MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
SS_MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=surakshasetu
SS_MINIO_SECRET_KEY=surakshasetu-dev-minio
SS_ANCHOR_RETENTION_DAYS=1
# Leave unset in dev (a dev key derived from a public constant signs). Outside dev: the path to an
# Ed25519 private key (PEM).
# SS_TSA_KEY_PATH=/path/to/tsa-ed25519.pem

# Model path (Steps 8-9). Chat routes go to compose's hardened OmniRoute (`make gateway-up`), which
# fronts the stubs; embed and rerank go straight to TEI. SS_GATEWAY_API_KEY is also the OmniRoute
# app key's value: `make gateway-up` imports it, so after changing it, rerun `make gateway-up`.
# All four required outside dev.
SS_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:20130/v1
SS_GATEWAY_API_KEY=surakshasetu-dev-gateway-key
SS_TEI_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081
SS_TEI_RERANK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082
# Bound to the embedding model in infra/compose.yaml: its vector size, and the instruction an
# instruction-tuned model needs before queries only (empty for BGE-M3). Change only with the model.
# SS_EMBED_DIM=1024
# SS_EMBED_QUERY_PREFIX=
# Dev and test only: multiplies the embed and rerank timeouts, because CPU TEI misses the TDD's GPU
# budgets (a 40-candidate rerank takes 20-40 s on CPU). Pilot and prod refuse anything but 1. The
# retrieval make targets set 1000 themselves.
# SS_TEI_TIMEOUT_SCALE=1

# Knowledge base (Steps 11-12): the three collections, written by ingestion, read by retrieval.
# Required outside dev.
SS_QDRANT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:6333

# Output rails (Step 14). The lexicon pack is content/lexicon/output-lexicon-<version>.yaml, picked
# at deploy time (not a session pin; every lexicon verdict records it). The sample rate is the share
# of S1-S2 (gen-converse) turns whose cited sentences go to verify-claims; S3 and side-queries
# always do. Both optional.
# SS_OUTPUT_LEXICON=2026.09.1
# SS_VERIFY_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1

# Transition rows (Step 15). The S2 -> S3 profile-sufficiency gate, the S3 -> S2 re-discovery loops
# allowed before Human Escalation, and the consecutive low-confidence turns that escalate (1 gives
# TDD §3.9's single-turn reading). Read at deploy time, not pinned per session. All optional.
# SS_PROFILE_SUFFICIENCY_MIN=0.7
# SS_REDISCOVERY_LOOP_LIMIT=2
# SS_LOW_CONFIDENCE_STREAK_LIMIT=2

# Logging. SS_LOG_DIR (unset: no files) adds one rotating JSON file per subsystem; text is a
# coloured console for local reading only.
# SS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# SS_LOG_DIR=../logs
# SS_LOG_FORMAT=json

# Test-only, not read from this file: `make check-db` and `make check-stack` export
# SS_TEST_PG_DSN_ADMIN, SS_TEST_PG_DSN_KEYVAULT and SS_TEST_PG_DSN_KB (app_rw on the dev database,
# for the retrieval stack test), built from infra/.env's passwords. The gateway
# stack tests need `make gateway-up` and script the stubs at SS_TEST_STUBS_URL (default
# http://127.0.0.1:8090).
